    "process_step": "#########\n# GDSC ETL is performed in two steps: shell script to ETL data into postgres\n# and then additional transformations with SQL in postGIS (if needed).\n####\n\n#########\n# Step 1 - bash script (pseudo code)\n####\n\n# create directory structure and move into it\nmkdir -p /data/mdc_2021_hylo/download -p /data/mdc_2021_hylo/mdc_2021_surface_temperature_30m/etl\nchmod -R 777 /data/mdc_2021_hylo\ncd /data/mdc_2021_hylo\n\n# set update flag based on last update and update frequency\ndo_update=0 if date() < last_update + update_frequency else do_update = 1\n\n# download if update flag is set:\nif do_update == 1 then\nwget --retry-connrefused --waitretry=1 --read-timeout=20 --timeout=15 -t 10 -O download/mdc_2021_hylo.zip 'https://scholarship.miami.edu/view/fileRedirect?instCode=01UOML_INST&filePid=13395678880002976&download=true' 2>&1\n\n# unzip to download directory if update flag is set\nif do_update == 1 then\nunzip -o download/mdc_2021_hylo.zip -d download && rm download/mdc_2021_hylo.zip 2>&1\n\n# load raster into postGIS with:\n    raster2pgsql -s 3857 -d -C -I -t 48x48 GeoTIFF_Rasters/Surface_Temperature_30m.tif -F mdc_2021_surface_temperature_30m > load_raster.sql\npsql <connection options> < load_raster.sql\nrm load_raster.sql\n\n# Move into corrrect directory and create derivative directory in data package on osgeo\ncd /data/mdc_2021_hylo/mdc_2021_surface_temperature_30m/\nmkdir -p derived\n\n# Move into correct directory\ncd /data/mdc_2021_hylo/mdc_2021_surface_temperature_30m/\n\n# Create pg_dump of table SQL in derivate directory on postgis.\npg_dump <postgres opts> -h gaia-db -t mdc_2021_surface_temperature_30m > derived/mdc_2021_surface_temperature_30m.sql\n\n# Create downloadable tarfile of SQL in derivative directory on postgis\nrm -f derived/mdc_2021_surface_temperature_30m.sql.tar.gz\ntar -czf derived/mdc_2021_surface_temperature_30m.sql.tar.gz meta_dcat_mdc_2021_surface_temperature_30m.json -C derived mdc_2021_surface_temperature_30m.sql\n\n",
